:   Whether to find rows whose text is nearly the same, as well as rows that are the same.

<code>[threshold]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [float]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [[0.8]{.fl}]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>

:   The smallest Jaccard similarity of two rows' word n-grams for them to be nearly the same
    (with `near=True`).

<code>[ngram]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [int]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [[5]{.dv}]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>

:   The number of words of the n-grams (with `near=True`).

<code>[num_perm]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [int]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [[128]{.dv}]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>

:   The number of MinHash permutations (with `near=True`).

<code>[drift_columns]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [str | list[str] | bool | None]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [None]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>

:   The columns to check for drift. By default, they're the numeric columns that the splits
    share and the others with few distinct values in the first split (at most 50, and at most
    half as many as its rows, which leaves out free text and identifiers), except for
    `label=`. Use `False` to check none.
